{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Those who banish you.</b> They drive you away, and [the root is as in] 'they shall thrust him' (Job 18:18). And some say: you are considered outcasts in their eyes." "And the meaning of <b>your brothers</b> is that it is harsher." "<b>YHWH will be heavy.</b> R. Moses the Kohen said that it is from the root of heaviness, and the meaning is that He is heavy upon him to mention Him and to keep His statutes. His proof is that [this root] is not found in the sense of honor except in the nif'al conjugation, like 'I am honored' (Isaiah 66:15 [sic]). But he forgot 'his sons will honor him' (Job 14:21), and the parallel is 'they will grieve him' [there]. Now according to his interpretation the meaning is clear, and תחס is a word of time, as if he said: I will yet bring a time when it will be seen in your joy and they will be ashamed — the words of those who banish. And thus the interpretation of the verse: your brothers said, for My name's sake, 'May YHWH be heavy; would that YHWH be heavy' — from the root of honor — 'and let it be seen in your joy, and we shall be ashamed.' And this is the meaning of 'and they shall be ashamed' — that they say that HaShem cannot show His glory. Now this verse connects with what comes after it. And the commentators said that [יכבד] is not the language of those who banish; they said it is the word of HaShem, in the manner of 'Let us make man' (Genesis 1:26) — and 'your brothers said' means HaShem and the prophet [said]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {0 "The Hebrew מנדיכם is Ibn Ezra's lemma from the verse; I render it as a participial phrase to match his interpretation.", 2 "Ibn Ezra's citation of Isaiah 66:15 for נכבדת appears erroneous; the form occurs at Isaiah 66:5 in some readings or at other verses. Retained as he cites it. The phrase דברי המנדים is read as marking the preceding as the banishers' words per his argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:16.989113804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}